  {
    "insert": "\n\nThis exposé proposes a Bachelor's thesis project exploring the integration of large language models (LLMs), specifically GPT-4, into introductory programming education. The focus is on using LLMs to automatically generate programming exercises aligned with Bloom's taxonomy, aiming to improve student engagement and learning outcomes. A split-study design involving two student groups—one using traditional materials and the other using LLM-enhanced content—is planned to evaluate the effectiveness of this approach. The exposé outlines the motivation, theoretical background, methodology, and timeline, using a LaTeX template and adhering to formal requirements.\n\n"
